  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Assistance to Conflict-Affected Ukrainians and Third Country Nationals Residing in Romania</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall objective of this initiative is to contribute to the wellbeing of conflict-affected populations in Romania. The intervention is designed to continue the provision of tailored assistance to both Ukrainians and third-country nationals (TCNs) who fled the war in Ukraine, in close cooperation with the Romanian Government. Through this project, IOM will work with specialized protection actors, including social services, to provide counselling, case management, and referral services to persons in vulnerable situations among the refugees and TCNs from Ukraine (e.g., older persons and persons with disabilities, children, including unaccompanied and separated children (UASC) women with children, persons with chronic health conditions, and those who have experienced or are at risk of violence, exploitation, and abuse, among others). The project also aims at increasing the engagement and inclusion of Ukrainians and TCNs with the host community by enhancing the capacities of a network of community centres that organize activities, conduct remote education and language courses, accumulate and disseminate information on available services, etc. Finally, the project will provide winterization support to conflict-affected population fleeing Ukraine by distributing non-food items (NFIs), hygiene items, health support and medicines, etc. at BCPs), transit and collective centers, and host communities.</narrative>
  </description>
